# Netlify SPA fallback — let the Angular router handle all client-side routes
# (auth, dashboard, admin, the dynamic /s/:slug public store, 404).
#
# index.csr.html is the route-agnostic client-rendering shell Angular's build
# generates alongside the prerendered pages — use it here, NOT index.html.
# index.html is the fully prerendered "/" (landing) page; if it were used as
# the catch-all fallback, deep-linking straight to e.g. /dashboard would
# briefly hydrate against the wrong (landing) DOM before the router corrects
# it. Netlify resolves an exact static file first (e.g. /privacy-policy/
# index.html) before falling through to this catch-all, so the prerendered
# marketing/legal pages are unaffected.
#
# Kept consistent with the [[redirects]] rule in netlify.toml.
/*    /index.csr.html   200
